@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: EXPERIMENT — should package-manager caches outlive a sandbox, and whose mechanism carries them?
' status: researched 2026-10-05, deferred on two upstream gates; nothing in src depends on this file
' would touch: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (GOPATH under _proveo_tool_home, _dep_lang_* table)
' would touch: internal/sbx/kit.go (no host-mount field today), internal/workspace/deps.go (DepLangs)
'   the persistence this rides today .. _spec/packages/lib/config-seeding-and-persistence.puml
'   the measure-first rule ............ _spec/_experiments/reusable-clone.puml
'   the Kit schema it would extend ..... _spec/_experiments/sbx-kit-capabilities.puml
'   the trees it must stay apart from .. _spec/packages/lib/dependency-trees.puml
'   upstream, pinned to PR #101's merge commit 129be2f:
'     docker/sandbox-kit-spec docs/spec/capabilities/com.docker.sandbox/host-mount@1.md
'     docker/sandbox-kit-spec examples/shared-cache/
'     docker/sandbox-kit-spec issues/96, pull/101, releases/tag/v3.0.0-m.8
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── THE QUESTION ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Every new sandbox re-downloads the same registry content. The tempting answer
' is to copy the HOST's caches (pnpm store, ~/go/pkg/mod, ~/.cargo/registry,
' ~/.cache/uv, ~/.m2, …) into the container per discovered language. Rejected:
'
'   SIZE      a host cache holds every project's history; a run needs one
'             lockfile's closure. Language discovery narrows the ecosystem,
'             not the packages.
'   PLATFORM  a macOS host caches darwin artifacts — macosx wheels, the
'             darwin @esbuild optional dep, GOOS-keyed build caches, compiled
'             gems. Same late failure dependency-trees.puml exists to stop.
'   SECRETS   ecosystem homes co-locate credentials: ~/.cargo/credentials.toml
'             inside CARGO_HOME, ~/.m2/settings.xml, ~/.gradle/gradle.properties.
'             A wholesale copy bypasses the broker.
'   TRUST     a copy is safe but paid every run; a rw bind lets the agent poison
'             the host's builds; a ro bind breaks managers that write.
'
' ── WHAT ALREADY CACHES, CHECKED 2026-10-05 ───────────────────────────────
'   sbx proxy         TLS interception, allowlist, credential injection. No
'                     response cache: `sbx settings list` exposes none, and
'                     platform.images.registryMirror covers Docker Hub images
'                     only (sbx v0.46.0; v0.47.0 notes are silent).
'   sbx sandbox disk  per sandbox, until `sbx rm`. Four sandboxes held 122 GB
'                     under sandboxd/containerd/root on the reference host.
'   proveo squid      cache_dir with no ssl_bump: HTTPS tunnels through
'                     uncached. Docker backend only.
'   proveo tool sync  toolchains/<os>-<arch>, restored by full copy into each
'                     fresh VM and saved at teardown. GOPATH lives under it, so
'                     Go's module cache (515 MB on the reference host) rides
'                     along. No other ecosystem's cache does — an asymmetry the
'                     language-uniform rule forbids, and a copy whose cost grows
'                     with every Go project the host has ever run.
'
' ── WHY WAIT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The work saves bandwidth, not correctness. Upstream ships NO cache, released
' or specified. It specified a STORAGE PRIMITIVE: docker/sandbox-kit-spec#96
' (2026-09-30) names the gap — "package and build caches like ~/.npm are
' sandbox-scoped, meaning every new sandbox re-downloads the same
' dependencies" — and PR #101 (merged 2026-10-02) adds
' com.docker.sandbox/host-mount@1: a runtime-owned host directory shared across
' one Kit's sandboxes, keyed by Kit identity + path, surviving sandbox removal,
' concurrent access without transactional guarantees.
'
' The split once it ships: sbx owns the persistent directory and its
' lifecycle; proveo still owns the CACHE — pointing each language's cache path
' at the mount. Building both halves now means proveo also owns host storage,
' lifecycle and cleanup that the primitive would hand to the backend.
'
' ── WHERE host-mount@1 STANDS, CHECKED 2026-10-05 ─────────────────────────
'   Kit spec    PRE-RELEASE. Ships in v3.0.0-m.8 (2026-10-02), a milestone
'               tagged prerelease. Spec v3 has run m.4 → m.8 since 2026-09-16;
'               no v3.0.0 final exists.
'   sbx 0.46.0  reads schemaVersion "2" Kits ONLY. `sbx kit validate` on the
'               upstream examples/shared-cache Kit fails before reaching the
'               capability: "field capabilities not found in type
'               spec.SpecFile; artifact validation failed".
'   sbx adapter PR #101: "the existing sbx adapter does not yet advertise this
'               capability".
'   sbx 0.47.0  release notes (2026-10-05) name neither host-mount nor spec v3.
'   proveo      Kits are schemaVersion "2" (internal/sbx/kit.go), so adopting
'               host-mount@1 is also a Kit migration to v3.
' No release date is published for spec v3 or for sbx support.
'
' ── SPEC RULES THAT SHAPE proveo's ADOPTION ───────────────────────────────
' From docs/spec/capabilities/com.docker.sandbox/host-mount@1.md:
'   * config is `path` (absolute, canonical, in-container) + optional `mode`;
'     there is NO host-path field — proveo cannot point it at a host cache,
'     which settles the host-copy question at the spec level too
'   * storage is keyed by Kit identity + path; a published repository supplies
'     the identity, an unpublished Kit gets a runtime-owned one — so where
'     proveo's Kits are built decides whether runs share one cache
'   * mounted before lifecycle hooks run, so the seed's installs can use it
'   * the same path declared by two Kits, or as host-mount@1 and volume@1,
'     CONFLICTS — one Kit owns each cache path
'   * filesystem semantics MAY be weaker than volume@1: host-mapped ownership,
'     no overlayfs upper layer or xattrs. Stores that hardlink into the
'     workspace (pnpm) must be probed, not assumed
'   * an `optional: true` group is SKIPPED by a runtime without host sharing,
'     and the manager falls back to its ordinary cache — the upstream
'     examples/shared-cache Kit pairs the mount with the manager's config file
'     inside one such group
'
' ── TRIGGER AND SHAPE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Two gates, in order; both must open:
'   1. sbx accepts schemaVersion "3" Kits.
'   2. sbx advertises com.docker.sandbox/host-mount@1.
' Check after each sbx upgrade:
'   sbx kit validate <dir holding examples/shared-cache/spec.yaml>   # gate 1
'   strings "$(readlink -f "$(which sbx)")" | grep -c 'host-mount@1' # gate 2
' Then, one row per DepLangs language inside optional groups, never one
' ecosystem first:
'
'   go      GOMODCACHE            rust  ~/.cargo/registry, ~/.cargo/git
'   node    pnpm store, ~/.npm    py    ~/.cache/uv, ~/.cache/pip
'   ruby    gem cache             jvm   ~/.m2/repository, ~/.gradle/caches
'
' and GOPATH leaves the tool sync, so the restore copies toolchains only. The
' host-mount is filled from inside the sandbox, so it is Linux-correct by
' construction and grows with what runs fetch, not with host history. Each
' client still checks content against its lockfile hashes (go.sum, pnpm
' integrity, Cargo.lock), which is what stands between one run's write and the
' next run's read. Credential files stay out: mount the cache subpath, never
' the ecosystem home.
title EXPERIMENT — package caches across sandboxes

actor "operator" as OP

node "host" as HOST <<host>> {
  database "host caches\ndarwin artifacts, every project,\ncredential files beside them" as HC <<db>>
  database "toolchains/<os>-<arch>\nGo module cache rides along" as TS <<db>>
  database "host-mount@1 dir\nKit-scoped, runtime-owned" as HM <<db>>
}

package "sbx VM, one per run" as VM {
  component "package managers\ngo · cargo · pnpm · uv · …" as PM
  database "sandbox-scoped caches\ngone at sbx rm" as SC <<db>>
}

cloud "registries\nproxy.golang.org · npm · crates · PyPI" as REG <<cloud>>
component "sbx proxy\nintercepts, never caches" as PROXY <<cloud>>
component "gate 1: sbx reads Kit v3\nCLOSED: 0.46 rejects v3" as G1 <<error>>
component "gate 2: adapter advertises host-mount@1\nCLOSED: not in 0.46 / 0.47" as G2 <<error>>

OP ARROW_MAIN PM : proveo run
PM ARROW_CLOUD PROXY
PROXY ARROW_CLOUD REG : every sandbox, same bytes
PM ARROW_QUEUE SC
TS ARROW_QUEUE PM : full copy per VM (Go only)
HC ARROW_ERROR PM : rejected: size, platform, secrets
HM ARROW_OPTIONAL G1 : spec v3.0.0-m.8, pre-release
G1 ARROW_OPTIONAL G2
G2 ARROW_OPTIONAL PM : optional group, skipped if unmet

note bottom of HC
  **Rejected as a source.** It scales with host
  history, holds darwin builds, and sits next to
  registry credentials. Discovery narrows the
  ecosystem, never the packages.
end note

note bottom of PROXY
  **No cache to lean on.** sbx's proxy exists to
  enforce policy and inject credentials; nothing
  in its settings or release notes caches a
  response.
end note

note bottom of TS
  **The asymmetry today.** GOPATH under the tool
  home makes Go the only ecosystem whose cache
  persists, and its restore copies the whole
  module history into each fresh VM.
end note

note bottom of HM
  **Storage, not a cache.** kit-spec PR #101,
  merged 2026-10-02; no sbx release has it.
  Filled from inside, so Linux-correct and sized
  by what runs fetch.
end note

note bottom of G1
  **Two gates, both closed.** sbx must first read
  schemaVersion "3" Kits, then advertise
  host-mount@1. proveo's Kits are v2, so adoption
  is also a Kit migration.
end note
@enduml
